[agent] The shift is unambiguous: daily mean holds at ~2.5 through 2026-02-25, then jumps to ~5.2 on 2026-02-26. Let me confirm with a change-point query computing the largest between-means gap.
[agent:bash] bq --project_id="$GCP_PROJECT" query --location="$GCP_LOCATION" --use_legacy_sql=false --format=pretty '
[agent:bash] WITH daily AS (
[agent:bash]   SELECT DATE(ts) day, AVG(prediction) m
[agent:bash]   FROM `'"$GCP_PROJECT.$GCP_BQ_DATASET"'.'"${MLPAB_GCP_PREFIX}"'_prediction_log`
[agent:bash]   GROUP BY day
[agent:bash] )
[agent:bash] SELECT day AS onset_day, ROUND(m,4) mean_today, ROUND(prev,4) mean_prev, ROUND(m-prev,4) jump
[agent:bash] FROM (SELECT day, m, LAG(m) OVER (ORDER BY day) prev FROM daily)
[agent:bash] ORDER BY ABS(m-prev) DESC LIMIT 3'
[agent:result] +------------+------------+-----------+--------+
[agent:result] | onset_day  | mean_today | mean_prev |  jump  |
[agent:result] +------------+------------+-----------+--------+
[agent:result] | 2026-02-26 |     5.2131 |    2.4854 | 2.7277 |
[agent:result] | 2026-03-13 |     5.3236 |    5.1477 | 0.1759 |
[agent:result] | 2026-02-19 |     2.6931 |    2.5445 | 0.1487 |
[agent:result] +------------+------------+-----------+--------+
