[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I logged and monitored the model's predictions on the platform (BigQuery feature store) and detected the distribution shift.
[agent] **What I did — all compute platform-side:**
[agent] 1. Loaded `data/prediction_log.csv` (13,483 predictions, Jan 1 – Mar 31 2026) into the per-run BigQuery dataset `mlpab_mlpab67bde5` as table `mlpab67bde5_prediction_log` (prefixed per the isolation rules).
[agent] 2. Ran BigQuery SQL to compute daily prediction statistics (count, mean, stddev) — the monitoring/statistics step.
[agent] 3. Ran a change-point SQL query over the daily means (LAG window) to locate the largest distributional jump.
[agent] **Finding:** The daily mean prediction sits steadily at ~2.5 (sd ~0.66) from Jan 1 through **2026-02-25**, then jumps to ~5.2 on **2026-02-26** and holds there through the end of the log. The day-over-day mean jump on 2026-02-26 is **+2.73**, roughly 15× larger than any other daily fluctuation (next largest ~0.18) — an unambiguous, level shift with no ambiguity in onset.
